# Unique Task Generation (strict)

Whenever asked to make **new** task ideas, specs, or `tasks/<name>/` drafts — or to **edit / revise / fix** a task — produce a design that is distinct on identity **and topology**, not wording. All nine primary categories are open; classify honestly.

Full one-shot prompt: `prompts/oneshot_unique_task.md`.

## Hard similarity gate

- **Maximum allowed similarity: 15%** (`0.15`) local and platform. Target **≤ 10%**.
- **> 15% is blocking** — new identity (domain, artifact, command, instruction voice, **env topology / layout_family**). Do not synonym-swap or rename modules in the same skeleton.

## Checker readiness (with uniqueness)

Uniqueness alone is not enough to ship. Also plant `@task-checker-ready.mdc`
floor (P1–P5), obey **`@checker-lessons.mdc`** (no recurring ship-killers), and
target checker complexity **medium or hard**. Difficulty metadata must be
`medium` or `hard` (never `easy`). See `prompts/TASK_CHECKER.md`.

## Evidence law (the usual failures)

Do **not** write a similarity percentage unless this turn's tool output contains a
`Max similarity:` line from:

```bash
python3 scripts/uniqueness_probe.py inventory
python3 scripts/uniqueness_probe.py probe --instruction /tmp/<slug>-instruction.md --exclude <slug>
python3 scripts/uniqueness_probe.py structure-plan --manifest /tmp/<slug>-structure.txt --exclude <slug>
python3 scripts/uniqueness_probe.py structure --task-dir tasks/<slug> --exclude <slug>
python3 ci_checks/check-similarity.py tasks/<task> --include-structure --enforce-threshold
```

A mental audit, “looks unique”, or a guessed `8%` is a policy violation.

**Instruction-only is insufficient.** Official Phase A2 uses `--include-structure`
(metadata + visible paths + test names). Real failure mode in this repo:
two Go tasks sharing `environment/cmd/driver/stages/` scored ~9% on prose and
**~78%** with structure. Authoring must pass instruction **and** structure
gates before polishing the rest of `tasks/<name>/`.

## Before inventing

1. Run `python3 scripts/uniqueness_probe.py inventory` and avoid occupied
   categories/outputs/commands/instruction heads/**layout_family**/**env_roots**.
2. Classify honestly (`.cursor/rules/submission-category-blocklist.mdc`).
3. Invent **≥ 3** candidates; keep one with **≥ 5** unique properties vs occupied set.
4. Probe final-voice instruction. Then `structure-plan` before creating the tree.
5. After skeleton exists, run `structure` + `check-similarity.py --include-structure`.
   If either FAILs, tear down topology; do not polish.

## Forbidden shallow variations

- CSV / log / ETL reshape that only swaps columns
- Debugging clone with a different bug in the same topology
- Software-engineering app that only swaps nouns or APIs
- API wrapper / report / converter reskin
- Clone-and-rename of an approved task **or** of a spec public contract
- House template: “Repair X under `/app` so `/app/bin/Y` regenerates
  `/app/output/Z.json`. Hand-written JSON is not enough…”
- **Same layout_family** (e.g. `go-cmd-driver-stages`) with renamed packages

## Never hide or relocate peer tasks

- Canonical path only: `tasks/<slug>/`. Never create `tasks/.peers/`,
  `tasks/.stash/`, or any other `tasks/.*` tree for tasks.
- **“Peer”** means another existing directory under `tasks/` — a word in
  uniqueness docs, not a folder to create.
- Do **not** `mv` / rename / copy other people's (or prior) tasks out of
  `tasks/<slug>/` to dodge similarity, free a slug, or “isolate” your work.
  Dot-directories are skipped by `check-similarity.py` / `check-task.sh`;
  stashing there is cheating the uniqueness gate.
- If `tasks/` already has peers, invent a **different identity** and keep
  peers where they are. Concurrent authoring shares the same `tasks/` tree.

## Policy phrasing

Say **maximum 15%** (not “10–15% band”). “≤ 10%” is the aspirational target only.
